[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":106},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":-5,"_42":43,"_44":45,"_46":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_54":36,"_55":56,"_57":58,"_59":36,"_60":61},"expiresAt",1795394442000,"id","v6t7o2gekhpdb4zls1sthkw2c","title","Bitdefender 揭示假 GTA VI 流客户端利用 ClickFix 投递 Windows 信息窃取木马","originalTitle","Fake GTA VI Streaming Client Installs Data-Stealing Malware on Windows PCs","summary","Bitdefender 发现网站 gta6cloud.nexus 以云端串流 GTA VI 为诱饵，通过 ZIP 下载或要求用户在 Win+R 中运行 PowerShell 命令投递恶意程序。","reason","source",{"_75":105},"links",{"_61":104},"publishedAt","2026-11-21T08:57:36.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-21T09:42:50.095Z","timelineAt","category","activity","tags",[78,76,102,103],"score",66,"selected",false,"channel","news","story",{"_86":87,"_13":88},"x","readingMode","full","author","Deeba Ahmed","body",{"_98":-5,"_61":99,"_100":-5,"_101":36},"outline",[89,90],"relatedStories",[85],"topics",[68,69,70,71,72],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group",{"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67},"hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original","factId","fOq4JKYjpIrg","reportCount",1,"additionalSourceCount",0,{"_73":83,"_75":84},{"_73":81,"_75":82},{"_73":79,"_75":80},{"_73":77,"_75":78},{"_73":74,"_75":76},"slug","malware","name","恶意软件","attack","攻击活动","black-market","数据窃取与黑产","ransomware","勒索软件","email","邮件与钓鱼",{"_86":87,"_13":88},"publicId","86efcf4e-cfa9-4d37-93ce-ae7345153cfb","虚假GTA VI云客户端窃取Windows凭据",{"_11":96,"_92":97,"_94":95},{"_11":91,"_92":93,"_94":95},"sec-2","text","A fake client hides a much bigger infection","level",3,"sec-1","How the attack works","zh","<p>Grand Theft Auto VI’s scams have not gone away with the game’s release. Hackread.com has previously reported fake <a href=\"https://hackread.com/grand-theft-auto-fake-gta-vi-beta-download-malware/\">beta downloads</a>, <a href=\"https://hackread.com/gta-6-early-access-websites-gamers-malware-crypto-scam/\">early-access offer</a>s and <a href=\"https://hackread.com/fake-gta-vi-download-sites-malware-launch/\">leaked-game </a>scams. Now, scammers are using the lack of an official PC version to deliver a fake streaming client that infects Windows computers with malware.</p><p>Bitdefender discovered this new scam after identifying a website (<code>gta6cloud.nexus</code>) claiming its GTA VI cloud client lets PC users stream the game from an Xbox or PlayStation. The catch here is that this site offers a ZIP download but also gives visitors another way to install it- asking them to press <code>Win+R</code>, paste a PowerShell command and run it.</p><h3 id=\"sec-1\"><strong>How the attack works</strong></h3><p>This is a ClickFix attack, where victims are tricked into running commands on their own computers. The command bypasses PowerShell’s execution policy, downloads a script from the site and runs it, eventually fetching and launching GTA6Cloud.exe.</p><figure><a href=\"https://hackread.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Fake-GTA-VI-Streaming-Client-Spreads-Rust-Based-Malware-to-Windows-Gamers.png\"><img width=\"975\" height=\"646\" src=\"/dailyinfo/media/99745244b21863f2.webp\" srcset=\"/dailyinfo/media/8f5818ff029b6034.webp 720w, /dailyinfo/media/ae5e3a2792e9b719.webp 1200w, /dailyinfo/media/99745244b21863f2.webp 1600w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1536px) 760px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 524px), (min-width: 640px) 608px, calc(100vw - 32px)\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"></a><figcaption>Fakw GTA VI client (Source: Bitdefender)</figcaption></figure><p>The fake client plays the GTA VI trailer and displays a game-themed page while downloading two more files, <code>loadperf.dll</code> and <code>unlodctr.exe</code>, from <code>velmontriq.net</code>. The files are placed in a hidden folder on the computer.</p><h3 id=\"sec-2\"><strong>A fake client hides a much bigger infection</strong></h3><p>The attackers use DLL sideloading to run their malicious code through unlodctr.exe, which is a legitimate Windows utility. A malicious DLL (<code>loadperf.dll</code>) is placed with it that gets loaded when the program runs. This gives the attackers a way to execute their code through a trusted executable.</p><p>Additionally, it contains another payload: <code>PhotoCache.exe</code>. This file is injected into legitimate Windows processes instead of being saved as a separate executable.</p><p>The injected payload is a Rust-based information stealer. In its <a href=\"https://www.bitdefender.com/en-us/blog/labs/fake-gta-vi-pc-client-malware-clickfix\">research</a> shared with Hackread.com, Bitdefender explained that it uses legitimate Windows tools and processes to stay hidden while collecting data from infected computers.</p><p>This includes browser passwords, cookies and tokens, Discord and Steam data, crypto wallets, AI service credentials and developer API keys. It can also access clipboard data and take screenshots. The malware sends stolen information to nimbuskeepcom and also attempts to connect to <code>192.30.240.26</code> on port <code>7777</code>.</p><p>This campaign takes a different approach from previously reported <a href=\"https://hackread.com/fake-gta-vi-download-sites-malware-launch/\">GTA VI scams</a> as it offers PC gamers an opportunity to stream the console version while they wait for an official PC release.</p><p>Anyone who ran the command should assume their computer is compromised. Bitdefender advises disconnecting it from the internet, scanning for malware and changing important passwords from a clean device, starting with email.</p>","zhKind","complete","钓鱼","数据窃取","https://hackread.com/fake-gta-vi-streaming-client-malware-windows-pc/","Hackread",{"_107":108,"_109":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
